title: February Revolution in Russia
subtitle: The Russian monarch has fallen.
view-if: month = 2 and year = 1917
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
	Q.russian_revolution = 1
	Q.soviet_relation = 50
!}
tags: event

= The February Revolution

After much instability in the previous months in Russia it has boiled over, and the Tsar has stepped down. With the Tsar's son refusing to take the throne, and the monarchy is over. 

A Provisional Government is formed, however the workers have formed their own councils. It is doubted that this situation will last long.

We could take advantage of this to print more pamphlets, though it may not be very effective due to resistance from the Party and suppression from the State.

- @pamphlets: Print pamphlets calling for revolution.
- @nothing: Do nothing.

@pamphlets
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!
	Q.resources -= 1
	Q.workers_spd += 3*(1-Q.dissent)
	Q.union_support += 4*(1-Q.dissent)
!}

@nothing
subtitle: Sometimes doing nothing is doing something.

In this case though it is nothing.